[size=6][b][color=#c9973f]InfinitePatch[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4]Modern PC fixes for BioShock Infinite.[/size]
[size=3]Borderless without alt-tab lag, no more crash after the intros, smooth high polling rate mice, UI scaling, wider FOV and more.
One [b].ini[/b] to configure, one click to apply, one click to undo.[/size]

[url=https://github.com/literalynn/InfinitePatch][b]Source code on GitHub[/b][/url]  ·  [url=https://github.com/literalynn/InfinitePatch/releases][b]Releases[/b][/url]  ·  [url=https://github.com/literalynn/InfinitePatch/issues][b]Report a bug[/b][/url][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#c9973f]Why InfinitePatch[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Fixes what nothing else does.[/b] The crash after the intro videos on PCs with an integrated GPU, the framerate drops with high polling rate mice, and the camera slowing down when you sprint.
[*][b]Several mods in one.[/b] Borderless, intro skip, UI scaling, wider FOV and graphics tweaks, all in one place and up to date for Windows 11.
[*][b]Your settings, not the game.[/b] No game file is modified. It edits the game's settings files and the Windows per-game graphics setting, plus one small [i]dinput8.dll[/i] for the fixes settings can't do.
[*][b]Fully reversible.[/b] Your original settings are backed up on the first install and [i]Uninstall.bat[/i] puts them back.
[*][b]Safe by design.[/b] An invalid value in the .ini is rejected with a clear message, and nothing is changed.
[*][b]Open source (MIT).[/b] Every release is built from the public code by GitHub Actions.
[/list]

