[size=4][b][color=#c9973f]Installation[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][b]Launch the game once, then close it.[/b] It creates its settings files on first launch.
[*][b]Extract the zip into the game's main folder[/b], the one that contains the [i]Binaries[/i] and [i]XGame[/i] folders. In Steam: right-click the game → [i]Manage[/i] → [i]Browse local files[/i]. This also puts [i]dinput8.dll[/i] in [i]Binaries\Win32[/i].
[*][b]Double-click Install.bat.[/b]
[/list]
[b]Run Install.bat again[/b] every time you edit [i]InfinitePatch.ini[/i], and after Steam updates or verifies the game: the game rebuilds its settings files when its own files change.

If Windows shows a security warning when you run [i]Install.bat[/i], click [i]More info[/i] → [i]Run anyway[/i]. To avoid it, right-click the zip → [i]Properties[/i] → tick [i]Unblock[/i] before extracting.

[b]Mod managers:[/b] install it manually. [i]Install.bat[/i] has to run once to apply your settings, which a mod manager can't do for you.

[size=4][b][color=#c9973f]Configuration[/color][/b][/size]
Everything lives in [i]InfinitePatch.ini[/i], with a description and the accepted values above each line. Edit it with Notepad, save, run [i]Install.bat[/i] again.
[spoiler]
[b]Display[/b]
[list]
[*][b]DisplayMode[/b]: 0 windowed, 1 exclusive fullscreen (vanilla), 2 borderless fullscreen (default)
[*][b]ResolutionX / ResolutionY[/b]: 0 = native resolution of your main monitor, or a size in pixels
[*][b]VSync[/b]: 0 off, 1 on (caps the game at your refresh rate)
[*][b]MaxFPS[/b]: 0 no limit, or a framerate limit
[*][b]UIScale[/b]: 0.0 vanilla to 1.0 full scaling with resolution
[*][b]FOVSliderRange[/b]: 15 vanilla, 50 = slider up to 105°, up to 100
[/list]
[b]Fixes[/b]
[list]
[*][b]ForceDedicatedGPU[/b]: runs the game on your graphics card
[*][b]FixHighPollingRate[/b]: fixes framerate drops with 1000 to 8000 Hz mice
[*][b]FixSprintSensitivity[/b]: same camera speed when you walk or sprint
[*][b]WindowedOptimizations[/b]: Windows 11 flip model for borderless (low latency, VRR, instant alt-tab)
[/list]
[b]General / Input[/b]
[list]
[*][b]SkipIntro2K, SkipIntroIrrational, SkipIntroUnreal, SkipIntroAMD[/b]: skip each intro video
[*][b]DisableControllers[/b]: ignores all controllers (fixes a spinning camera caused by DS4Windows, ViGEm, vJoy)
[/list]
[b]Graphics[/b] (keep the game's setting by default)
[list]
[*][b]LensFlares, DepthOfField, MotionBlur, HighQualityLightShafts[/b]: -1 keep, 0 off, 1 on
[*][b]ShadowResolution[/b]: 0 keep, or 1024 / 2048 / 4096 / 8192 (Ultra is 2048)
[/list]
[/spoiler]

[size=4][b][color=#c9973f]Compatibility[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Steam version[/b]: made and tested with it. GOG and Epic Games Store use the same game files and should work (the Epic settings folder is detected automatically).
[*][b]Sprint sensitivity fix[/b]: current Steam build only (May 2022). It turns itself off on any other version.
[*][b]Other dinput8.dll mods[/b]: can't run at the same time as the native fixes. [i]Install.bat[/i] tells you when that's the case.
[*][b]Windows 10 and 11[/b]. Windowed game optimizations need Windows 11.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#c9973f]Uninstall[/color][/b][/size]
Double-click [i]Uninstall.bat[/i]. It removes [i]dinput8.dll[/i] and restores the settings files and the Windows graphics setting saved during the first install. You can then delete the remaining InfinitePatch files from the game folder.

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#c9973f]Troubleshooting[/color][/b][/size]
[spoiler]
[b]The game crashes on startup[/b]
Close overlay and monitoring tools before launching the game: MSI Afterburner / RivaTuner Statistics Server, the NVIDIA overlay and the Discord overlay.

[b]My settings went back to default[/b]
The game rebuilds its settings files after an update or a file verification on Steam. Run [i]Install.bat[/i] again.

[b]"Game settings not found"[/b]
Launch the game once, close it, then run [i]Install.bat[/i] again.

[b]The camera spins on its own, or I see Xbox buttons with a keyboard and mouse[/b]
Set [i]DisableControllers = 1[/i] in [i]InfinitePatch.ini[/i], then run [i]Install.bat[/i] again.

[b]I changed the display mode in the game's options[/b]
The game's own options still work and take priority until you run [i]Install.bat[/i] again.
[/spoiler]

[b]Found a bug?[/b] Use the Bugs tab or [url=https://github.com/literalynn/InfinitePatch/issues]GitHub issues[/url], with your Windows version, GPU and what happened.

[line]

